    "body": "## Summary\n- give proposal-acceptance top-ups a dedicated, recoverable Stripe return contract\n- route redirect-based methods to an authenticated proposal-payment recovery page instead of the transient details-page state\n- remove Stripe `payment_intent`, `payment_intent_client_secret` and `redirect_status` from the address bar before asynchronous recovery while keeping only non-secret refresh context\n- resume from the requester-only server funding preflight and call the existing authoritative proposal-accept endpoint only after webhook-funded balance is visible\n- treat browser redirect status as informational only; a reported failure still receives a server funding check before recovery stops\n- add dependency-free frontend tests for return URL construction, validation and secret scrubbing\n- document redirect recovery, privacy and settlement invariants\n\n## Financial / marketplace invariants\n- Stripe webhook still only credits the normal wallet `TOP_UP` ledger path\n- webhook never selects a worker or mutates proposal state\n- final proposal acceptance still revalidates owner, job/proposal state, blocks, wallet and escrow atomically on the backend\n- failed/stale marketplace acceptance leaves any successfully credited Stripe money in the requester's wallet\n- no schema change / no Flyway migration required\n\n## Validation\nMerge only after every latest-head CI and payment/runtime smoke run is completed successfully.",
